VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T09:19:20Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T11:48:38Z","body":"> We could expand this assert to headers by making the template reusable. The easiest way would probably be `__COUNTER__`; while technically non-standard, it's de facto standard like `#pragma once` and `alloca()`. Not sure if there's a use-case for that right away, but I can see it being handy as the includes become more fine-grained\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I understand, could you expand on the idea?\r\n\r\nEdit: Ohh, I think I get it. You mean probably something like this, right? (pseudocode)\r\n```c++\r\n// <my_header.h>\r\nbool was_already_incomplete = is_incomplete_type_v<Type>();\r\n\r\n#include \"abc.h\"\r\n#include \"def.h\"\r\n#include \"gi.h\"\r\n\r\nif (!was_already_incomplete && is_incomplete_type_v<Type>()) {\r\n    #error \"Class was incomplete etc.\"\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2979603711/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_